WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.198 --> 00:00:20.204
The next morning Ben and Sid arrived at the show bright and early.

2
00:00:20.224 --> 00:00:24.626
"First, we have to clean some cages," Ben said.

3
00:00:24.646 --> 00:00:27.747
He led Sid over to some empty chairs.

4
00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.108
"You can wait here.

5
00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:32.989
I'll do the cleaning myself, just in case you're allergic to anything.

6
00:00:33.609 --> 00:00:36.090
When I'm done, I'll get you, and we can visit the rats."

7
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:37.610
"Sounds good."

8
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:38.751
Sid nodded.

9
00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:41.371
"Cleaning cages doesn't sound fun anyway."

10
00:00:41.391 --> 00:00:43.632
"It's not," Ben agreed.

11
00:00:46.593 --> 00:00:49.874
About an hour later, the brothers approached the rodent area.

12
00:00:50.414 --> 00:00:53.635
Almost instantly, green spots appeared on Sid.

13
00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:59.813
He tried holding a hairless mole rat, but even that one caused green spots to appear.

14
00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:06.016
Finally, Sid threw up his hands in frustration.

15
00:01:06.036 --> 00:01:09.897
"We've tested dogs, lizards, dragons, and now rats!"

16
00:01:10.598 --> 00:01:12.318
He looked like he was about to cry.

17
00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:16.680
"Maybe we should try snakes after all, even though I hate them."

18
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.641
"Maybe," Ben said.

19
00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:22.663
But he wasn't crazy about a pet snake either.

20
00:01:22.683 --> 00:01:25.764
"Look, there's Waldo.

21
00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.393
He's got Oswald with him."

22
00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.453
Ben waved his friend over.

23
00:01:29.473 --> 00:01:30.414
"Hey, guys!"

24
00:01:30.774 --> 00:01:33.355
Waldo smiled as he hurried over with his owl.

25
00:01:33.755 --> 00:01:35.336
He held up Oswald's cage.

26
00:01:35.356 --> 00:01:37.817
"I think I've got this guy's problems worked out.

27
00:01:38.057 --> 00:01:39.898
He's been following all my commands today."

28
00:01:39.918 --> 00:01:43.899
"But Sid stared at the cage and blinked.

29
00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:46.520
"That cage is empty, Waldo."

30
00:01:47.481 --> 00:01:48.841
Ben and Waldo chuckled.

31
00:01:48.861 --> 00:01:55.744
"It's not empty," Waldo said, clapping a hand on Sid's shoulder.

32
00:01:56.664 --> 00:01:59.686
"Oswald is an invisible owl," Ben explained.

33
00:01:59.706 --> 00:02:01.728
"He can make himself disappear."

34
00:02:01.748 --> 00:02:03.769
"Wow, he's invisible?

35
00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:08.432
Cool!" Sid pressed his face right up against the bars of the cage.

36
00:02:10.553 --> 00:02:12.875
Then he turned around to flash a grin at Ben.

37
00:02:12.895 --> 00:02:14.956
"Look! No spots!

38
00:02:15.437 --> 00:02:17.338
We can get an invisible owl for a pet!"

39
00:02:17.358 --> 00:02:20.980
"Unless your spots are invisible too," Ben said.

40
00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:22.922
Sid scratched his head.

41
00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.763
"Oh good point."

42
00:02:25.703 --> 00:02:26.164
"Watch this.

43
00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.961
I'll make Oswald visible," Waldo said.

44
00:02:29.461 --> 00:02:31.141
He let out two sharp whistles.

45
00:02:33.282 --> 00:02:33.902
They waited.

46
00:02:33.922 --> 00:02:38.143
"I still don't see him," Sid said.

47
00:02:38.703 --> 00:02:40.424
Waldo frowned and whistled again.

48
00:02:42.985 --> 00:02:44.625
But again nothing happened.

49
00:02:45.385 --> 00:02:46.746
Ben tried whistling next.

50
00:02:50.107 --> 00:02:52.207
Still there was no sign of the owl.

51
00:02:52.227 --> 00:02:54.568
"Maybe he's asleep."

52
00:02:55.348 --> 00:02:56.929
Waldo reached into the cage.

53
00:02:56.949 --> 00:02:58.510
"Hey, Oswald, wake up!"

54
00:02:59.151 --> 00:03:02.053
He felt around for a moment before turning back to Ben.

55
00:03:02.073 --> 00:03:04.315
"Uh-oh." He sounded worried.

56
00:03:04.335 --> 00:03:06.476
"I think Oswald escaped."

57
00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:10.519
"What?" Ben stared at Waldo in disbelief.

58
00:03:10.539 --> 00:03:11.900
"Are you sure?"

59
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.442
"Yes!" Waldo nodded.

60
00:03:14.462 --> 00:03:16.283
"He's not in his cage!"

61
00:03:16.303 --> 00:03:18.685
"When was the last time you saw him?"

62
00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:19.726
Sid asked.

63
00:03:20.046 --> 00:03:22.628
"Er I mean, you know what I'm trying to ask."

64
00:03:25.236 --> 00:03:27.797
"I was practicing with him in the library," Waldo said.

65
00:03:27.817 --> 00:03:30.278
"He was visible when I put him back in the cage.

66
00:03:30.758 --> 00:03:32.618
Then I went to the cafeteria for a snack.

67
00:03:33.498 --> 00:03:34.739
Maybe he escaped somehow then."

68
00:03:34.759 --> 00:03:36.559
"Did you lock the cage?"

69
00:03:36.899 --> 00:03:37.640
Ben asked.

70
00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:41.001
"I thought I did," Waldo said with a shrug.

71
00:03:41.021 --> 00:03:43.901
"But maybe I forgot or the latch was loose or something."

72
00:03:44.762 --> 00:03:46.302
He held his face in his hands.

73
00:03:46.322 --> 00:03:47.983
"This is terrible."

74
00:03:48.863 --> 00:03:51.604
Ben took a deep breath, trying to stay calm.

75
00:03:53.336 --> 00:03:55.418
"He's probably still inside the school building.

76
00:03:55.738 --> 00:03:56.799
Let's start looking for him."

77
00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.721
"How do you look for an invisible owl?"

78
00:04:00.042 --> 00:04:00.822
Sid asked.

79
00:04:01.723 --> 00:04:03.805
"I have no idea," Ben said.

80
00:04:03.825 --> 00:04:05.486
"But we're about to figure that out.

81
00:04:06.727 --> 00:04:07.368
Come on, Waldo."

82
00:04:08.068 --> 00:04:09.590
The wizard just stood there.

83
00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:12.232
"What if he flew outside?"

84
00:04:12.692 --> 00:04:13.513
Waldo moaned.

85
00:04:13.533 --> 00:04:16.035
"If that happened, he'll be lost forever!"

86
00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:19.598
"We haven't even looked yet, Waldo," Ben said.

87
00:04:19.618 --> 00:04:21.980
"And now we're losing precious time."

88
00:04:22.824 --> 00:04:28.766
Waldo nodded, and the three monsters began searching, whistling and calling for the missing owl.

89
00:04:34.447 --> 00:04:38.228
They searched all over the gym and then looked in some classrooms.

90
00:04:39.269 --> 00:04:41.989
Next they checked the library and hallways.

91
00:04:42.009 --> 00:04:47.851
"I told you this was hopeless," Waldo said.

92
00:04:47.871 --> 00:04:50.992
"There's no way to find an animal who's invisible!"

93
00:04:51.744 --> 00:04:54.185
Ben stayed quiet, and so did Sid.

94
00:04:54.685 --> 00:04:56.666
It was hard to argue with Waldo's point.

95
00:04:57.386 --> 00:05:00.308
Then Ben spotted Miss Bungle waving madly at him.

96
00:05:00.328 --> 00:05:02.068
"There you are, Ben!

97
00:05:02.649 --> 00:05:04.089
I've been looking for you.

98
00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.651
You were supposed to sweep the bunny rabbits' area.

99
00:05:09.071 --> 00:05:10.092
You didn't show up."

100
00:05:11.292 --> 00:05:12.153
"Oh, right.

101
00:05:12.473 --> 00:05:13.473
Sorry, Miss Bungle!"

102
00:05:13.753 --> 00:05:14.493
Ben replied.

103
00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:20.256
"Waldo's owl um, well, we had a small emergency."

104
00:05:21.244 --> 00:05:25.047
"You should get going," Miss Bungle said, glancing at her watch.

105
00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:28.769
"You don't want to miss the pet tricks show when it starts."

106
00:05:28.789 --> 00:05:31.531
"Go ahead, Ben," Waldo said.

107
00:05:31.551 --> 00:05:33.833
"Sid and I will keep looking for Oswald.

108
00:05:34.093 --> 00:05:35.154
You can catch up with us later."

109
00:05:35.694 --> 00:05:36.415
Ben nodded.

110
00:05:37.756 --> 00:05:40.938
It probably wouldn't take him long to sweep the bunny rabbits' area.

111
00:05:41.558 --> 00:05:44.280
After that he could rejoin the hunt for the missing owl.

112
00:05:44.861 --> 00:05:49.524
A chill rippled along his spine as he remembered the owl's sharp beak and talons.

113
00:05:51.285 --> 00:05:53.761
He hoped Oswald wasn't busy hunting right now!
